{"login": "tomblah", "location": null, "commits": [{"sha": "0e26883487bac1c3ca028277ef5e0402423a1af9", "message": "Minor project structure cleanup", "created_at": "2021-11-28T08:35:01Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "df4fa7a3e0a3b0dcb1d486ef317c646c1e199429", "message": "Don't show sort options until starships have loaded\n\nNB: This is a quick fix as I've just noticed this right before submission. Happy to neaten up the code if required.", "created_at": "2021-11-28T08:23:02Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6a9a9b32495fc4ec4ccd6dd3f0f88d062849d299", "message": "Adding a README", "created_at": "2021-11-28T08:23:02Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b8a43446a406bcc9225da4de3bca98e6eae09f4e", "message": "Starship details\n\nHere we make a screen to show the starship details when the user taps on a starship from the main list.\n\nThe presenter calls the router which then configures the details scene.\n\nIn the details screen we have the same basic layout as the cells in the main list, but we simply show more details.\n\nNB: there is a room to add much more fields on the screen, but I'm guessing that fully fleshing out this screen is not the main point of the exercise :-).\n\nNB: I've noted with `TODO`s the stuff I would refactor if it were a real life project.", "created_at": "2021-11-28T07:32:36Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2bf776637c003dcc2b4518ca1d26a081b7adf5b4", "message": "Show starships in a list\n\nHere we take the retrieved `Starship`s and show them in a collection view. We use a collection view as opposed to a table view as it's more future proof e.g. it's plausible that the next stage of development might be to show the starships in a carousel.\n\nWe show the following properties in the list:\n\n* Name\n* Manufacturer\n* Cost (if available)\n\nAnd allow the user to tap a \"star\" button to favourite a starship. We store the favourites (in memory) in the `AppManager`. To change to persistable is simple as making the `Starship` codable and writing custom getters and setters for `favouritedStarships` to write to `userDefaults`.\n\nThe `Starship`s are sortable by tapping the sort button in the top right. We've chosen a random subset of `Starship` properties as supported sort options for demonstration purposes.\n\nThe business logic (loading, favouriting, sorting etc.) is done in the presenter while the display logic is done in the view controller. NB: when a user taps a favourite button, we have a handler in the cell that calls the delegate function `didToggleFavourite` -- the view controller conforms to `StarshipListCollectionViewCellDelegate`, but simply passes the call to the presenter to handle the business logic.\n\nNB: due to time constraints there's various critical things that I dropped -- I've noted these as `TODO`s.\n\nWe've included another 3rd party library: `ActionSheetPicker-3.0` to use for our sort order selection.", "created_at": "2021-11-28T05:31:43Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "030c25f750413a47480b84cbfbb2f79796c4d065", "message": "Get starships from API\n\nHere we wire up the API to get the starships from: `https://swapi.dev/api/starships/`.\n\nWe do manually do the parsing of the JSON into our `Starship` model.\n\nWe user `Alamofire` to make the simple network call and `SwiftyJSON` to parse the result.\n\nIMPORTANT: in a real life situation we most likely wouldn't be using `SwiftyJSON` and instead the model objects and the parsing code itself would be automatically be generated from an `OpenAPI` doc.", "created_at": "2021-11-27T06:17:31Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2c4633e2b36d66b1b7bb98e1cc5fa929646407a7", "message": "Project setup\n\nSetting up the project for the code challenge:\n\n* Adding `.gitignore`\n\n* Using Cocoapods (will initially use `TinyConstraints` for programmatic layout, `Reveal` for UI debugging and `SVProgressHUD` for loading indicators).\n\n* Removing Storyboard\n\n* Adding the initial screen (blank at the moment)\n\n* Adding some misc things like a `UIColor` extension that probably be useful shortly, an `AppManager` singleton and a `Starship` model.", "created_at": "2021-11-27T05:21:10Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ccfacb73b4f3bcbf45752b590319c62e8842add7", "message": "Initial Commit", "created_at": "2021-11-26T05:08:14Z", "repo": "StarWarsStarships", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f71096b8e14f8369464ee017b0e8f754ee33c553", "message": "Merge branch 'feat/dependencies-update'", "created_at": "2025-09-28T01:22:53Z", "repo": "auto-prompt-generator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6f2b5b67ef8786844a85c7bec1be83381f1420a8", "message": "Cargo update", "created_at": "2025-09-28T01:22:42Z", "repo": "auto-prompt-generator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ee005cb123242b2c95551994c577fb700c449550", "message": "Merge branch 'feat/dependencies-update'", "created_at": "2025-07-08T13:04:21Z", "repo": "auto-prompt-generator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "62c655ae75b2b22a84dc3eb6d6206fa316d99d70", "message": "Cargo update", "created_at": "2025-07-08T13:04:12Z", "repo": "auto-prompt-generator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d88cb0e846918e5c9b2e366c754b34707ed30d49", "message": "Merge branch 'feat/dependencies-update'", "created_at": "2025-05-09T10:18:37Z", "repo": "auto-promp